ge his contribution if he succeeds.'], 'decision_authority': 'Full authority to assign this task. Ability to adjust team priorities for the upcoming week to compensate for this extra work.'}, 'fullname': '彭冲', 'avatar': ''}, 'actor_role': {'name': 'Junior Wang', 'gender': 'Male', 'description': 'A talented and ambitious junior engineer who has been with the company for two years. He is a fast learner and highly motivated but can sometimes rush through his work, leading to careless mistakes in the details.', 'age_range': '23-26 years old', 'identity': 'Junior Software Engineer', 'education_level': "Bachelor's Degree", 'work_experience': '2 years of professional experience, all at this company.', 'background': {'actor_know_facts': "Wang feels he's ready for more responsibility and has been hoping for a high-visibility project to prove his worth. However, last month he pushed a minor update that caused a small bug because he skipped a testing step, and he got some light criticism for it. He is now a bit more cautious about high-stakes tasks. It's his anniversary this weekend, and he has made special, non-refundable dinner and hotel reservations.", 'actor_unknow_facts': "The manager is under immense pressure from the director. This task is seen by upper management as a key test of the new manager's ability to deliver through their team."}, 'relationship_to_user': 'You were his senior colleague and informal mentor before you became his manager. The relationship is generally positive, but the dynamic is still new.', 'interaction_history': "You've done code reviews for him in the past, often catching small, careless errors.", 'related_history': 'This is the first time you are delegating a task of this magnitude and urgency to him since becoming manager.', 'communication_history': 'Communication has always been friendly and informal.', 'goals': ['To understand what the manager wants and figure out if he has to cancel his weekend plans.', 'To seize this as an opportunity to 